session: benchmark

**Ref:** `session/status/benchmark.md` §20.29-30 (full detail).

**Resume prose:**

Continuation of the same-day resume (§20.24-29): the coder session picked back up after an app
restart, found a completed live `make benchmark-run` (`m-ta-prefill-knee` profile) on disk, and a
fresh handoff from a *sibling* coder session on this same branch/worktree reporting a live-cluster
problem — an orphaned `m-ta-calibration-probe` run (killed by a local session interruption, no
usable data ever produced) left decode stuck at **10/10 replicas with zero load** after a
`reset_run.py --apply` cleanup restarted the controller.

Verified the stuck state directly against the cluster (WVA logs showed `demand=0, util=0, rc=0`
but `desiredReplicas` pinned at 10, not converging) and freed the GPUs via the documented
`free_gpus` pattern (pause ScaledObject at 0, scale decode to 0) — confirmed 0 pods left.
**10 H100s released on the shared cluster.**

Root-caused and fixed the `postprocess.py` bug §20.29 had flagged and left for input: it only ever
read guidellm's `results.json`, but the current harness (inference-perf) writes
`summary_lifecycle_metrics.json` instead, so P99 TTFT/ITL and error count silently degraded
(error count was showing a **wrong** 0, not just a missing value — a real failure existed).
Separately fixed `_extract_queue_depth_avg`'s stale EPP pod-name filter and metric name. Fix
supports both harness formats (not a replacement) per direction. Verified against the real run,
not just compiled — all three fields now populate correctly.

Three commits: `66c71f8e` (land the run's 5 allowlisted files), `6a10f458` (the postprocess.py
fix), `eee20e33` (regenerated REPORT.md with correct values). Branch now 30 commits ahead of
`origin/benchmark`, all local, DCO-signed, nothing pushed.

**Owed by Dean:** nothing blocking. Worth knowing about: (a) the orphaned calibration-probe run's
setup-only PVC directory (`/requests/inference-perf-1786538941-lwy8cw_1`) is harmless and was left
in place, not deleted; (b) the `m-ta-calibration-probe` cell itself has still never produced usable
data — worth a clean re-run whenever convenient, now that the toolchain and the GPUs are both in a
known-good state.

**No footguns armed.** GPUs are freed and verified (ScaledObject paused at 0, deploy at 0 replicas,
zero pods) — the standard "un-pause before the next run" reminder applies as always. Sibling
session's handoff marked `.DONE`.

**CURRENT.md update suggested:** fold into the existing benchmark abstract — note the postprocess.py
fix (both harness formats now supported, a real error-count miscounting bug fixed), the idle-GPU
incident and resolution, and point at §20.29-30 rather than restating detail.
